/* Talk mode — Mandarin Chinese: 80 spoken dialogs, from 你好 to telling the story of learning it.
   Sixteen themes of five levels. 1–40 (survival): greetings → café & restaurant → numbers &
   shopping → directions & transport → hotel & problems → small talk → plans & invitations → past,
   health, opinions, story. 41–80 (holding a conversation): work & study → phone & online →
   telling stories → opinions & disagreeing politely → feelings & helping people → everyday admin
   → culture, food & life here → longer conversation.
   Pinyin marks the tone changes of 不 and 一 (bú shì, yí gè); 3 + 3 is written as dictionary tones
   (nǐ hǎo, said ní hǎo). See content/chinese/TALK.md. */
